<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21859" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impĕrātōrĭus</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inp-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		imperator. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			general</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quod ipse honos laborem leviorem faceret
					imperatorium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 2, 26, 62</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Verr. 2, 1, 21, § 57</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">partes (shortly before: imperatoris partes),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 3, 51, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 11, 4, 1</span></i>
			; 
			
			<i><span class="en">Tac. A. 1,
			3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consilium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 3, 6, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ac. 2, 1, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virtus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 7, 10, 13</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">8, 2, 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ars,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					2, 17, 34</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">manubiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					de Or. 3, 3, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulvis sudorque (opp. campestris meditatio),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Pan. 13, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">navis,</span>”
				<i>an admiral's ship</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 1, 5, § 22</span></i>
			.—* <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impĕrātōrĭē</span></b> ,
				<i>like a general</i>: dum se ad id bellum
			imperatorie instruit, Treb. <i><span class="en">Claud.
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(Acc. to imperator, II. B. 3.) <i>Imperial</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genesis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Dom. 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">munera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Vesp. 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">onera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Calig. 42</span></i>
			.</div>
